  rules: [
    ['BR-01', 'Immutable identifiers', 'Patient numbers are generated by the system and never change; accessions are sequential per visit; sample IDs are unique and never reused.'],
    ['BR-02', 'Tube merge', 'Services with the same clinical group, sample type and sample condition share one sample; any difference splits them.'],
    ['BR-03', 'Received gate', 'A result may not be recorded until the sample status is Received (auto-receive emulates it in Release 1).'],
    ['BR-04', 'Profile completion', 'A profile or package reaches Complete, Reviewed or Verified only when every member test has.'],
    ['BR-05', 'Reserved keeps the bill', 'Deferring a service keeps it in the visit and the bill with no sample; cancelling removes it from both.'],
    ['BR-06', 'Contract sets the price', 'Payer and contract tier determine every service\'s patient share and payer share.'],
    ['BR-07', 'Three-layer pricing', 'Base list price × tier factors = contract price; Apply propagates base-list changes to all derived tiers except excluded services.'],
    ['BR-08', 'Patient condition selects the range', 'Reference ranges resolve by sex, age and patient condition.'],
    ['BR-09', 'Verify is a signature', 'Verification records who signed and when; only verified results print.'],
    ['BR-10', 'Not-X queue logic', '"Not X" returns everything below X in the test track.'],
    ['BR-11', 'Delta check warns', 'A delta flag must be investigated and acknowledged but does not block verification.'],
    ['BR-12', 'Frequency check', 'A repeat order inside the configured interval alerts or is prevented.'],
    ['BR-13', 'Turnaround clock', 'Expected result = collection + duration counting only test days; delay colours are a percentage of the duration consumed.'],
    ['BR-14', 'Negative balance means refund', 'A negative visit balance is returned through the refund flow, never above the refundable amount.'],
    ['BR-15', 'Nothing is erased', 'Cancellations, transfers, rejections and edits keep the original data with reason, user and time.'],
    ['BR-16', 'Drawer equation', 'Expected cash = cash payments − refunds; card and transfer amounts are not in the drawer.'],
    ['BR-17', 'Group privileges propagate', 'Changing a role changes every user in it; changing one user affects that user only.'],
    ['BR-18', 'New sample, new barcode', 'A replacement sample carries a new barcode unless the tenant policy allows reinstatement.'],
    ['BR-19', 'Default list value is not a result', 'The default of a list test is empty or a placeholder, never a value that reads as a result.'],
    ['BR-20', 'Hidden helpers', 'Helper tests feeding formulas or sums never print.'],
    ['BR-21', 'Percentage tolerance is a multiplication', 'A ±20 % tolerance is written as × 0.8 and × 1.2 of the live range values.'],
    ['BR-22', 'Every boundary needs its complement', 'A rule for one side of a boundary needs a condition or complement so other patients are not stopped.'],
    ['BR-23', 'No last result must not stop', 'Rules using the previous result must not stop patients who have none in the window.'],
    ['BR-24', 'Validated selection only', 'Fields that reference master data accept only selected values.'],
    ['BR-25', 'Tenant copy of master data', 'A tenant\'s master data is an independent copy of the global templates; later global changes follow the update policy.'],
    ['BR-26', 'Payment inside registration (Release 1)', 'The amount captured on the registration page is recorded with the visit on save; it may not exceed the amount due; non-cash payments need a reference.'],
    ['BR-27', 'Treasury per device (withdrawn)', 'Withdrawn on 2026-10-20 (LIS-CR-004): a money movement is stamped with the cashier, the session branch, the payment method and its reference; no cash drawer or device approval is required.'],
    ['BR-28', 'Sign-in by address', 'Each laboratory signs in only at its own address (<base>/lab/<slug>) and the Super Admin only at <base>/admin/login; a user who is not a member of the laboratory of the address, or not platform staff at the admin address, is refused exactly like a wrong password. After sign-in the session carries the laboratory; signing out or timing out returns to the same address.'],
    ['BR-29', 'Collected outside per sample', 'Whether a sample was collected outside the laboratory is recorded per sample (tube), not per visit: such a sample is Collected at the time typed at registration whatever the auto-collect parameter says, still waits for its receipt, prints EXT on its label and marks the visit "ext" in lists.'],
    ['BR-30', 'Closed cash period is read-only', 'Once a cashier (or a branch) closes a period, no payment, refund or cash entry may be posted or voided inside it (BIL-061); the next ledger opens with the counted cash of that close.'],
    ['BR-31', 'Subscription grace', 'A laboratory whose trial ended without activation, or whose wallet has been at or below zero for a plan period, runs a grace period (platform parameter, default 7 days) with reminders; when it ends only its administrators may sign in, to the wallet (SUB-020 / SUB-021). Reminders are sent once per threshold.'],
    ['BR-32', 'Report design precedence', 'The design of a printed result report is the payer contract tier\'s when set, else the report template\'s, else the laboratory\'s Printing parameter (Classic by default).'],
  ],

